From 83ccbc35a8c97c910fdd964a1097c9978bf669ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Lane A <lane-a@local.invalid>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 11:25:35 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(edl): cut, zoom and transition only where the
 footage gives a reason

Root cause of clip1.mp4 (handoff/quality-clip1/ROOT_CAUSE.md): build_edl
sliced clips into equal intervals by cuts-per-minute (Gaming: 21 slices in
58 s), snapped them to the beats of the music bed the app adds, punched in
every 12 s ("rehook"), pushed in over the opening and flashed on the bed.

auto_director/content_cuts.py, behind EDL_CONTENT_CUTS (default OFF until
Luffy approves the corrected render, per Sanji Q15):
- segments start only at a source shot change (clip["scene_cuts"], from
  detect_clip_scene_cuts: scene > 0.25 over the clip window; 0.4 found none
  of the real cuts in the clip1 venue footage, which score 0.28-0.36) or a
  sentence end; cuts-per-minute is a ceiling; min shot 2.5 s;
- no interval or automatic opening zooms; an energy punch needs speech
  under it, max one per 8 s, not in the first/last second;
- the signature transition only on a real shot change;
- a beat grid that follows the added music bed is not applied (no snapping
  or flashing to decoration); source-audio grids still apply;
- every decision recorded under edl["edit_restraint"].
video_service and the phase-2 harness pass the clip's scene cuts.

Evidence (same 141-199 s window): handoff/quality-clip1/step1/ (render,
before/after, cut list with reasons, ffprobe, render log).
Tests: test_content_cuts 7/7. With the switch off the existing edit suites
are unchanged; 8 render tests fail identically on 996d074 (Windows drawtext
paths, NVENC hatch) and test_pipeline_edl_honours_classifier_and_fallback
fails on 996d074 too once assets/music is populated (Auto bed applies).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
